---
description: Names and folders of the UI code
globs: src/**/*.ts, src/**/*.tsx
alwaysApply: false
---
A plan that breaks this file is a conflict, whether or not behaviour changes: stop the dependent work and report it.
src/naming-layout.test.ts checks what a file listing can decide.

| Under `src/features/<feature>/` | Holds | File names |
|---|---|---|
| `index.ts`, `client.ts` | public API, for Server Components and for Client Components | as named |
| `proxy.ts`, `phone.ts`, `public.ts`, `session-sync.ts`, `constants.ts` | narrow entries, each for a stated reason | as named; a new entry needs a row here first |
| `components/[<area>/]` | React components, and the hooks and helpers only they use | `<thing>-<kind>.tsx`, one component per file, exported under the PascalCase of the file name |
| `lib/[<area>/]` | logic with no JSX | the words below |
| `schemas/[<area>/]` | zod schemas and the rules they share | `<thing>.schema.ts`, `<thing>-policy.ts` |
| `services/` | calls to the API, and transports | `<thing>-api.ts`; a transport is named for what it does |
| `types/` | types over the generated client | `index.ts`, or `<thing>.ts` |
| `session/` | the session, in auth only | |
| `data/` | static page content, in marketing only | |

| Word | Means |
|---|---|
| `-flow.ts` | the steps of one user action, dependencies injected, no JSX |
| `-form.ts` | one form without JSX: values, checks, request body |
| `-form.tsx` | the component of a form |
| `-model.ts` | turns API data into what a screen shows. Existing `-view.ts` files do the same and keep their names; new code uses `-model.ts`, so that `-view` means a component |
| `-state.ts` | a state shape and the pure steps that change it, URL state included |
| `-text.ts` | turns a code or a value into display text |
| `-api.ts` | the calls of one API group |
| `-context.tsx` | a React context and its hook |
| `-provider.tsx` | a component that gives a context its value |
| `-view.tsx` | the client root of a page |
| `-dialog`, `-panel`, `-section`, `-step`, `-card`, `-notice`, `-list` | what the user sees |
| `use-<thing>.ts` | one hook, beside the components that use it, or in `lib/` when more than one folder does; no `hooks/` folder |
| `*.test.ts`, `*.test.tsx`, `*.test-support.ts` | a test beside the file it tests (`.test.tsx` renders a component in jsdom), and helpers for tests |
| `*.server.ts` | server-only code |

A new word needs a row here first. Existing names outside these tables stay; new code follows them.
